BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Barcelona//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Barcelona — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pa amb tomàquet — Toasted bread rubbed with half a ripe tomato\, then olive oil and salt.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa am too-MA-ket. The gesture that opens every Catalan meal\; nobody can say who first did it. Best: Quimet & Quimet\, Poble Sec — under the conservas
LOCATION:Quimet & Quimet\, Poble Sec — under the conservas
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Quimet+%26+Quimet+Poeta+Cabanyes+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:La bomba — A fist of mashed potato round spiced meat\, fried and capped with hot sauce and allioli.
DESCRIPTION:Say: la BOM-ba. Barcelona's own bar invention\, credited to María Pla's kitchen in Barceloneta in the 1950s. Best: La Cova Fumada\, Barceloneta — the original\, cash only
LOCATION:La Cova Fumada\, Barceloneta — the original\, cash only
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Cova+Fumada+Carrer+del+Baluard+56+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arròs Parellada — Rice in the paella pan with every shell and bone already taken out.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-ROSS pa-ra-LYA-da. Made\, the story goes\, about 1902 for a Barcelona dandy who would not peel a prawn. Best: 7 Portes\, Passeig d'Isabel II — its signature since 1836's room went kitchen
LOCATION:7 Portes\, Passeig d'Isabel II — its signature since 1836's room went kitchen
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=7+Portes+Passeig+d%27Isabel+II+14+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Canelons — Pasta tubes filled with roast meat\, under béchamel and gratinéed.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ka-ne-LONS. Italian by birth\, Catalan by ritual: every family eats them on Sant Esteve\, 26 December. Best: Can Culleretes\, Barri Gòtic — the house recipe
LOCATION:Can Culleretes\, Barri Gòtic — the house recipe
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Culleretes+Quintana+5+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Crema catalana — Cooked custard scented with cinnamon and lemon under a sugar crust broken with the spoon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KRE-ma ka-ta-LA-na. A custard is in the fourteenth-century Sent Soví\, long before the first French brûlée recipe. Best: Can Culleretes\, Barri Gòtic — since 1786
LOCATION:Can Culleretes\, Barri Gòtic — since 1786
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Culleretes+Quintana+5+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Suquet de peix — Fishermen's stew of fish and potatoes\, thickened with a pounded picada of nuts and garlic.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-KET de PESH. Born of the bony fish nobody would buy\; the name means 'to give off juices'. Best: Els Pescadors\, Poblenou
LOCATION:Els Pescadors\, Poblenou
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Els+Pescadors+Placa+de+Prim+1+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Patatas bravas — Fried potatoes under allioli and a hot sauce.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-TA-tas BRA-vas. Every bar has them\; the Sarrià version\, allioli and hot oil apart\, is the one the city argues for. Best: Bar Tomás\, Sarrià
LOCATION:Bar Tomás\, Sarrià
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Tomas+Carrer+Major+de+Sarria+49+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tortillitas de camarón — Lacy fritters of tiny shrimp\, crisp to the edge.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tor-tee-LYEE-tas de ka-ma-RON. A Cádiz plate the Raval learned at the long bar over the open kitchen. Best: Bar Cañete\, El Raval — at the counter
LOCATION:Bar Cañete\, El Raval — at the counter
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Canete+Unio+17+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Montadito of salmon and truffled honey — A small open sandwich of smoked salmon\, yogurt and truffled honey\, eaten standing.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mon-ta-DEE-to. The house's own construction\, built from the tins on its walls since 1914. Best: Quimet & Quimet\, Poble Sec
LOCATION:Quimet & Quimet\, Poble Sec
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Quimet+%26+Quimet+Poeta+Cabanyes+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Fried fish\, the four tapas — Small fried fish\, anchovies\, botifarra and a tomato-onion salad: the whole menu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pesh-KAH-to. The same four plates since 1945\, at a marble counter in the Gothic. Best: Bar La Plata\, Barri Gòtic
LOCATION:Bar La Plata\, Barri Gòtic
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+La+Plata+Merce+28+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Steak tartare on marrow bone — Hand-cut steak tartare laid on a split\, grilled marrow bone.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tar-TAR. The original of a plate that is now copied across Spain\, from 2012. Best: Suculent\, El Raval
LOCATION:Suculent\, El Raval
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Suculent+Rambla+del+Raval+43+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Xampanyet — The cloudy\, faintly sweet house sparkling wine\, poured from the bottle.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sham-pa-NYET. The bar took its name from it in 1929\; drink it with the house anchovies. Best: El Xampanyet\, El Born
LOCATION:El Xampanyet\, El Born
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=El+Xampanyet+Montcada+22+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vermut — Red vermouth with ice\, an orange slice and an olive\, with tins and crisps.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ver-MOOT. Fer el vermut: Barcelona 'does' a vermouth at noon on a weekend\, it does not just drink one. Best: Bar Bodega Quimet\, Gràcia
LOCATION:Bar Bodega Quimet\, Gràcia
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Bodega+Quimet+Vic+23+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cava — Traditional-method sparkling wine from the Penedès grapes Macabeu\, Xarel·lo and Parellada.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KA-va. First bottled by Josep Raventós at Codorníu in 1872\, an hour inland. Best: Can Paixano\, by the port — the glass for about a euro
LOCATION:Can Paixano\, by the port — the glass for about a euro
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Paixano+Reina+Cristina+7+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Xarel·lo — The Penedès white grape made as a serious still wine.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sha-REL-lo. The backbone of cava\, now bottled on its own by the growers who left the appellation. Best: Bar Mut\, Eixample — ask the counter
LOCATION:Bar Mut\, Eixample — ask the counter
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Mut+Pau+Claris+192+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Natural wine — Low-intervention bottles from Catalan growers\, by the glass.
DESCRIPTION:Say: vee na-too-RAL. Barcelona has one of Europe's deepest natural-wine lists in a single room. Best: Can Cisa / Bar Brutal\, El Born
LOCATION:Can Cisa / Bar Brutal\, El Born
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Brutal+Barra+de+Ferro+1+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Suizo — Spoon-thick hot chocolate under a cap of whipped cream.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SWEE-tho. Poured in the room that says it invented Cacaolat\, open since 1870. Best: Granja M. Viader\, El Raval
LOCATION:Granja M. Viader\, El Raval
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Granja+M+Viader+Xucla+4+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panellets — Almond-paste sweets rolled in pine nuts\, for All Saints.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-ne-LYETS. Per Tots Sants\, castanyes i panellets: 1 November\, with chestnuts and sweet wine. Best: Escribà\, La Rambla — the 1902 shop\, shut for the Rambla works from January 2026: check first\, or any pastisseria in late October
LOCATION:Escribà\, La Rambla — the 1902 shop\, shut for the Rambla works from January 2026: check first\, or any pastisseria in late October
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Escriba+Rambla+83+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Convent sweets — Marzipan\, yemas and biscuits made by enclosed nuns across Spain.
DESCRIPTION:Say: dool-SES de con-VENT. Eaten in a candlelit basement over the remains of a medieval bathhouse. Best: Caelum\, Barri Gòtic
LOCATION:Caelum\, Barri Gòtic
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caelum+Palla+8+Barcelona
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:barcelona-liste-20@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Calçots amb romesco — Long sweet onions charred black\, peeled by hand and dipped in romesco.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kal-SOTS am ro-MES-ko. From Valls\, about 1898\; the season is January to March\, so book it ahead for a winter trip. Best: A calçotada in Valls\, Alt Camp — winter only
LOCATION:A calçotada in Valls\, Alt Camp — winter only
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Valls+Catalonia
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
